Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma of left breast FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FOCAL SLIGHTLY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received unfixed   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a suture designating the axillary region  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 17 5cm tan white skin ellipse with a central unremarkable nipple  8 0cm lateral to the nipple is a 2 5cm linear  well healed scar  The anterior aspect of the specimen is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm cavity containing surgical clips positioned in the lateral aspect of the specimen  The cavity is lined by dense white fibrous tissue with a 0 5cm yellow  firm mass at the superior aspect of the cavity  The cavity lies 2 0cm from the posterior margin  Lymph nodes are not identified within the axillary soft tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest black inked deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of unremarkable parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue that may represent lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section adjacent to biopsy cavity  Fellow Review by Paul N Staats M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final