Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  None provided  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   0 2 CM FROM MARGINS  2  RADIAL SCAR  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SKIN  ADDITIONAL RIGHT MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  SCAR  CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR SURGICAL PROCEDURE  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right breast simple mastectomy specimen  which is unoriented  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm portion of white skin with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm nipple areolar complex with a centrally located 1 6cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  There is a 4 5cm in length crescent shaped  well healed scar on the skin surface  which extends to the nearest skin margin  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cavity  which is located subjacent to the scar on the skin surface  and appears to abut the posterior margin  The cavity has a smooth tan pink lining and is surrounded by dense gray white fibrous tissue with multiple metallic clips  There are also focal areas of tan yellow fat necrosis identified  Within the lobulated fat between the scar on the skin surface and the cavity is a dense gray white fibrous area with multiple cystis  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with a scant amount of interspersed gray white fibrous tissue  No other masses or lesions are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity to nearest margins  with section to skin scar in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from cavity  Received fresh  labeled  additional right mastectomy flap   is a 9 5cm in diameter rim of white  wrinkled skin excised to a depth of 0 6cm  There are no masses or lesions identified on the skin surface  The margins are inked black  and representative sections are submitted in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Skin  Additional Right Mastectomy Flap   Excision  report_end  , Positive.
